Day 45/120 – Mastering DAX Time Intelligence (Cheat Sheet Edition)

Today I focused on one of the most powerful parts of data analysis in Power BI — Time Intelligence in DAX.

Instead of just calculating totals, I learned how to make my data tell a story over time. Here’s what I covered:

📌 First & Last Order Dates
	•	Used MIN and MAX with CALCULATE to identify the start and end of sales activity
	•	Helps define the data range and business timeline

📌 Previous Month Sales
	•	Leveraged PREVIOUSMONTH() to compare current performance with the last month
	•	Key for spotting short-term trends

📌 Month-over-Month Growth (MoM)
	•	Combined DIVIDE and SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR() logic
	•	Learned how to calculate percentage growth and track performance changes

📌 Parallel Period Comparison
	•	Used PARALLELPERIOD() to shift time context (e.g., same period last year)
	•	Super useful for year-over-year comparisons

📌 Year-To-Date (YTD)
	•	TOTALYTD() helped me track cumulative performance from the start of the year

📌 Month-To-Date (MTD)
	•	TOTALMTD() gave insight into current month progress